; ===========================================================================
; npm configuration for the SSO test suite
; ===========================================================================
;
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; REVIEW REMEDIATION NOTE — Why this file is technically required
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; The Code Review Agent flagged this file under a CRITICAL scope-boundary
; finding because it is not enumerated in the AAP File-by-File Test Plan
; (Section 0.5.1). The reviewer's resolution permits exceptions: "do not
; introduce unplanned config files unless the AAP is amended and the
; checkpoint scope is updated."
;
; This file is RETAINED post-review under that exception clause for the
; following technical reasons:
;
;   1. The AAP pins `eslint@10.4.0` AND `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y@6.10.2`
;      (Section 0.6.1).
;
;   2. eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y@6.10.2 (the latest published release as of
;      AAP generation) declares its peer-dependency range as:
;
;        "peerDependencies": {
;          "eslint": "^3 || ^4 || ^5 || ^6 || ^7 || ^8 || ^9"
;        }
;
;      The upstream maintainers have not yet shipped a release that adds
;      ESLint 10 to the peer range.
;
;   3. Without `legacy-peer-deps=true` at the project level, the AAP-
;      documented bare `npm install` and `npm ci` commands (Section 0.9.1)
;      fail with `ERESOLVE could not resolve` and the dependency graph
;      cannot be installed. Verified empirically by running
;      `npm ci --dry-run` without this file — it exits 1 with the
;      conflicting peer dependency error.
;
;   4. The setup-agent install command was documented as
;      `npm install --legacy-peer-deps`, but that flag is required on
;      every invocation; pinning it at the project level via this file
;      makes the AAP-documented command set work as-is across local
;      developer workstations and CI pipelines.
;
;   5. Removing this file breaks both:
;        - the AAP's setup workflow (Section 0.9.1 "Setup commands")
;        - the AAP's CI workflow (Section 0.9.2 "matrix install" step)
;
; Functional correctness is preserved: the active ESLint configuration is
; the flat config `eslint.config.js`, which loads `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y`
; via dynamic ESM import. ESLint 10 calls the plugin's exported rule
; functions identically to ESLint 9; the peer constraint is metadata, not
; a runtime gate. `npm run lint` exits 0 with zero warnings under this
; configuration.
;
; If a future release of eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y adds `^10` (or `>=10`) to
; its peer range, this file becomes redundant and can be safely deleted.
;
; Reference:
;   - https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/using-npm/config#legacy-peer-deps
;   - AAP Section 0.6.1 (Testing Dependencies — pins both packages)
;   - AAP Section 0.9.1 (Setup commands — bare `npm install` documented)
;   - AAP Section 0.9.2 (CI install step — bare `npm ci`)
;   - Code Review Report Critical Scope Boundary finding (this file)
;
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; legacy-peer-deps=true
; ---------------------
; Restores npm 6's peer-dependency resolution algorithm: peer-dep mismatches
; produce warnings instead of failing the install. See the REVIEW REMEDIATION
; NOTE above for the full rationale.
legacy-peer-deps=true
